  "body": "First slice of #1448: a user-set **start point** on closed 2D Contour rings.\n\n## What changed\n- `motion::approach::Approach` gains `start_point: Option<Point2>` (validated finite and within 1 km at command creation).\n- New `motion::machining2d::contour_start`: the ring nearest the pick starts at the pick's projection onto the cutter-centre path, on every level; the lead-in is planned there. Refused by name, never moved silently: a pick farther than 1.5 tool diameters + stock to leave from every ring; no lead-in fitting at the pick; tabs; control / wear compensation. The automatic seam logic (axis start, control seam, lead-room reseat) moved into the same module unchanged.\n- `contour_along_chain` (open chains) refuses a pick by name.\n- App: `named_refusal` refuses a pick on a tilted contour and on every other kind; project file writes `links.approach.start_point` only when set; the params digest grows only when set. MCP `edit_operation` reaches it through the existing merge patch (no new tool needed).\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/1448-contour-start-point.md`.\n\n## How tested\n- `crates/motion/tests/contour_start.rs` (6): picked start on every level + perpendicular lead at the pick, no pick = default path move for move, far pick / NaN / tabs / control comp / open chain refused by name. Unit tests in `contour_start.rs` (2).\n- `crates/app/tests/contour_start_point.rs` (6): door refusals (NaN, inf, 2e6, tilted), EditOperationParams + undo/redo, project round-trip (key only when set), stamp, MCP `edit_operation` (contour taken, pocket refused), new golden `golden/contour_start_point.cl` (no existing golden touched).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` clean; `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main` green on 075921bfa: motion suites 208 s, app suites 1548 s, ui suites 143 s, 0 failed (no existing golden changed).\n\n## Not exercised\n- No UI row and no viewport pick: the parameter is set through MCP or the project file for now (owed in #1473). No look seen in a running app.\n- A refusal for \"no lead-in fits at the pick\" is coded but not pinned by a fixture that triggers it.\n- Exit points, pocket/adaptive entry placement, open chains, tabs/compensation/tilt with a pick: follow-up #1473.\n\nChangelog: Contour: an optional start point (`links.approach.start_point`, MCP `edit_operation`) starts the nearest closed ring at the picked spot, refused by name where the lead law cannot hold it (#1448)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nRefs #1448\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
